<%#
  The care receiver's side of a telephone conversation: "go to remindly dot
  care slash start, and type these six numbers."

  Its own layout, no navigation, and the field is the only thing on the page —
  whoever is typing is being talked through it by somebody who cannot see their
  screen.
%>
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
  <div class="text-center">
    <%# A real label rather than a heading that looks like one.

        The field had no accessible name at all: a screen reader announced "edit
        text, blank" on the one page in this product whose entire job is typing
        six numbers somebody is reading to you down a telephone — with impaired
        vision being part of why the telephone is the channel. Making the
        instruction the label means the visible words are the announced words,
        which is better than a hidden duplicate that can drift from them. %>
    <%= label_tag :code, "Type your six numbers", class: "block text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8" %>

    <% if flash.now[:alert] || flash[:alert] %>
      <p id="code_help" class="text-2xl text-gray-700 mb-8"><%= flash.now[:alert] || flash[:alert] %></p>
    <% else %>
      <p id="code_help" class="text-2xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
        The person setting this up will read them to you.
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <%= form_with url: start_path, method: :post do |f| %>
      <%# inputmode numeric so a tablet shows a keypad rather than a keyboard,
          and autocomplete off so a previous code is never offered back.
          aria-describedby carries the sentence under the label, so somebody
          hearing the page is told who will read the numbers out. %>
      <%= text_field_tag :code, nil,
            inputmode: "numeric", pattern: "[0-9]*", autocomplete: "off",
            autofocus: true, maxlength: 6, required: true,
            "aria-describedby": "code_help",
            class: "w-64 text-center text-5xl font-bold tracking-widest border-4 border-gray-300 rounded-xl py-4 px-3" %>

      <div class="mt-8">
        <%= submit_tag "Start", class: "btn-primary text-2xl px-8 py-6", data: { disable_with: nil } %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
